  "body": "Closes #560\nRefs #360 (left: the LOT-005 `smiley-search` oracles; LOT-053/LOT-155 specs keep their « pending » lines)\nRefs #124 (left: a banned or deleted member's profile; the smiley file name with a space, read but not published)\nRefs #388 (left: a message on a later MP page)\nRefs #337 (capture backlog; not found this batch: #111 #113 #121 #438 #1002; skipped (need a write or a state user2 lacks): #112 #115 #118 #119 #276 #613; #476 not done)\nClaim: mac/M1\nAuthor model: Claude Opus 5.5 (mac/M1-capB-opus)\nReviewer model: Fable 5.1 (ezzz-hfrnow.mac-m1.reviewer.captures-b, mac/M1-review-capB-fable-r2)\n\n### What\nCapture batch B of the #337 backlog, 2026-11-18: read-only GETs (anonymous or the user2 capture account; one login POST; never user1; 20 s apart; 31 requests). Fragment `corpus.d/337-batch-b-20261118.json`, MANIFEST rows (with « Not captured » rows), HFR-PROTOCOL bullets.\n\n- #360: 9 smiley-search captures (`R360a`-`R360i`): `%20` ORs words, a literal `+` narrows (AND not proven exact), accents, logged-out identical, wiki page of an unknown code (no entry form); `R360h` (wiki of a known code, logged in) published **meta only**.\n- #124: `R124p1` a logged-in profile with a status other than « Membre ».\n- #388: `R388a` meta only: a `cat=prive…&numreponse=M` link answers 200 in place (not R25's 301).\n- #560: `T560a`/`T560b` meta only (Giphy media URL without query; search without `lang`).\n\n### Anonymizer\nTwo positions the redactor and the verifier both missed, found by the author's own leak check: a pseudo with **raw spaces** (da15de8a) and with an **apostrophe** in raw, `&#039;` or `&apos;` form (13a467df) in the posts-by-pseudo path `/hfr/recherche/pseudo-…htm`. Tests in `tests/test_positions.py`, each red without its layer.\n\n### Checks\n- `anonymize.py check --corpus` 759/759 clean; fixture tests 403 OK; manifest agrees; pre-commit.\n- Leak checks: the author's script (0 findings) and Fable's independent harvest (rounds 1 and 2: no pseudo, id, token, key or MP subject survives; R54 checked too). The batch republishes byte-identically with the operator's standard `local.json` (no private config needed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n",
